# THE SIFREI ROWS on Deuteronomy 1:9-17 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 1 — THE OPENING SPEECH, 2026-09-15): piskaot 9-17 by POSITION — on 1:9
# (9), 1:10 (10), 1:11 (11), 1:12 (12), 1:13 (13), 1:14 (14, no citation at its head), 1:15-16 (15), 1:16 (16), 1:17 (17); forty-four rows,
# each read in both files; the middah named. The shelf's Hebrew cut by consonants (deu_ink.SP_).
from deu_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(9, 1, 'CONTEXT', '"AND I SAID TO YOU AT THAT TIME, SAYING" — NOT FROM MYSELF BUT FROM THE MOUTH OF THE HOLY ONE. The refrain.')
srow(9, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"I CANNOT BEAR YOU ALONE" — COULD MOSES NOT JUDGE ISRAEL? THE MAN WHO BROUGHT THEM OUT, SPLIT THE SEA, BROUGHT DOWN THE MANNA, DROVE THE QUAIL — COULD NOT JUDGE THEM? RATHER: "THE LORD YOUR GOD HAS MULTIPLIED YOU" (1:10) — BEYOND YOUR JUDGES. SO SOLOMON: "GIVE YOUR SERVANT A HEARING HEART" (1 Kings 3:9) — COULD SOLOMON NOT JUDGE? RATHER: I AM NOT LIKE OTHER JUDGES — A KING OF FLESH AND BLOOD JUDGES TO DEATH AND IT IS NOTHING TO HIM, TAKES TWO SELAS FOR ONE; I, IF I WRONGLY CHARGE MONEY, AM CLAIMED IN MY SOUL — "THE LORD WILL PLEAD THEIR CAUSE AND DESPOIL OF SOUL THOSE WHO DESPOIL THEM" (Proverbs 22:22-23). THE JUDGE\'S LIABILITY ROW ({SP_(9, 2, "אם", "חיבתי", "ממון", "נפשות", "אני", "נתבע")} "if I wrongly charged money, I am claimed in souls") — \'I cannot\' read not as incapacity but as the weight of judging; the compile\'s judge (the judge liable in his person for a money error — Proverbs 22:23 the rule\'s seat).')
srow(10, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND BEHOLD YOU ARE TODAY AS THE STARS OF HEAVEN FOR MULTITUDE" — YOU ENDURE AS THE DAY. HENCE: SEVEN CLASSES OF THE RIGHTEOUS IN THE GARDEN OF EDEN, ONE ABOVE THE OTHER (Psalms 140:14, 65:5, 84:5, 15:1 twice, 24:3 twice). ({SP_(10, 1, "שבע", "כתות", "של", "צדיקים", "בגן", "עדן")} "seven classes of the righteous in the Garden of Eden") — \'today\' read \'as the day\' (the sound), the seven classes by seven psalm clauses.')
srow(10, 2, 'CONTEXT', 'R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: THE FACES OF THE RIGHTEOUS WILL BE LIKE SEVEN JOYS — THE SUN, THE MOON, THE FIRMAMENT, THE STARS, THE LIGHTNINGS, THE LILIES, THE TEMPLE\'S LAMPSTAND (Judges 5:31, Song 6:10, Daniel 12:3 twice, Nahum 2:5, Psalm 45:1, Zechariah 4:3). The seven likenesses.')
srow(11, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE LORD GOD OF YOUR FATHERS ADD TO YOU A THOUSAND TIMES" — THEY SAID: MOSES, WE DO NOT WANT YOUR BLESSING! THE OMNIPRESENT PROMISED ABRAHAM "AS THE STARS AND AS THE SAND" (Genesis 22:17), AND YOU SET A LIMIT? A PARABLE: THE KING LEFT HIS YOUNG SON A GUARDIAN; GROWN, THE SON ASKED FOR HIS FATHER\'S SILVER AND GOLD; THE GUARDIAN GAVE FROM HIS OWN FOR HIS KEEP — WHAT I GAVE IS MINE; WHAT YOUR FATHER LEFT IS KEPT. SO MOSES: "A THOUSAND TIMES" IS MINE; YOURS — "AND BLESS YOU AS HE SPOKE TO YOU": AS THE SAND, THE PLANTS, THE FISH, THE STARS. THE GUARDIAN PARABLE ({SP_(11, 1, "זו", "משלי", "ושלכם", "ויברך", "אתכם", "כאשר", "דבר")} "this is from mine, and yours — \'and he bless you as he spoke\'") — read before by topic in gen_29 (enrichment there) — named, not fresh; the two halves of 1:11 as two blessings: Moses\' bounded, the LORD\'s unbounded; the outside row 82:5 the same verse refused as a lengthening of the priestly blessing.')
srow(12, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"HOW CAN I BEAR ALONE YOUR TROUBLE" — THEY WERE TROUBLESOME: ONE SAW THE OTHER WINNING AND SAID: I HAVE WITNESSES TO BRING, PROOFS TO BRING, TOMORROW I PLEAD, ADD JUDGES. ({SP_(12, 1, "יש", "לי", "עדים", "להביא", "יש", "לי", "ראיות")} "I have witnesses to bring, I have proofs") — the litigant who delays; the three words of 1:12 as three faults (12:1-3).')
srow(12, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOUR BURDEN" — THEY WERE HERETICS (EPICUREANS): IF MOSES WENT OUT EARLY — WHY? PERHAPS HIS HOUSE IS NOT IN ORDER; LATE — HE SITS PLOTTING AGAINST YOU, LIKE THE HOUSE OF ON (Numbers 16:1). ({SP_(12, 2, "מלמד", "שהיו", "אפיקורסים")} "it teaches that they were Epicureans") — the burden read as slander of the leader; the translation\'s \'your business\' keeps the plain sense.')
srow(12, 3, 'CONTEXT', '"AND YOUR STRIFE" — THEY WERE DISPUTATIOUS: ONE PAID A MANEH TO TAKE TWO, TWO TO TAKE THREE. The third fault (the English notes the small-type text is missing in manuscripts).')
srow(12, 4, 'CONTEXT', 'ANOTHER WORD: "YOUR TROUBLE, YOUR BURDEN, YOUR STRIFE" — EARLY: HIS HOUSEHOLD GATHERS THE COARSE MANNA; LATE: HE ATE, DRANK AND SLEPT; IN THE MIDDLE: HE WANTS US TO RISE; AT THE SIDE: HE UPROOTS THE RISING FOR AN ELDER. MOSES: IN THE MIDDLE I DID NOT SATISFY YOU, AT THE SIDE I DID NOT. The slanders of every step.')
srow(13, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"GIVE YOURSELVES" — "GIVE" IS COUNSEL ("GIVE YOURSELVES COUNSEL", 2 Samuel 16:20; "COME, LET US DEAL WISELY", Exodus 1:10). ({SP_(13, 1, "אין", "הבו", "אלא", "עצה")} "\'give\' is nothing but counsel") — the imperative fixed from its other seats (E7); the ink: \'give yourselves\' four seats, Ahithophel\'s among them.')
srow(13, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"MEN" — DID WE THINK OF WOMEN? WHY "MEN"? IN CUTTING AND IN MOSAIC — SEASONED AND FIT MEN. ({SP_(13, 2, "אנשים", "ותיקים", "וכשרים")} "seasoned and fit men") — the exclusion read from \'men\' (I2\'s exclusion), the judges\' first quality.')
srow(13, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"WISE" — ARIOS ASKED R. YOSE: WHO IS WISE? HE WHO KEEPS HIS LEARNING. OR IS IT THE UNDERSTANDING MAN? "AND UNDERSTANDING" IS ALREADY SAID. THE WISE IS LIKE A RICH MONEY-CHANGER: WHEN THEY BRING HIM COINS HE EXAMINES, WHEN NOT HE BRINGS OUT HIS OWN; THE UNDERSTANDING LIKE A POOR ONE: WHEN NOT, HE SITS AND WONDERS. THE TWO MONEY-CHANGERS ({SP_(13, 3, "חכם", "דומה", "לשלחני", "עשיר")} "the wise is like a rich money-changer"; {SP_(13, 3, "נבון", "דומה", "לשלחני", "עני")} "the understanding is like a poor money-changer") — the two qualities distinguished by the parable; the compile\'s judge: two competences named.')
srow(13, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND KNOWN TO YOUR TRIBES" — KNOWN TO YOU: ONE WRAPS IN HIS CLOAK AND SITS BEFORE ME AND I DO NOT KNOW HIS TRIBE, BUT YOU KNOW HIM, YOU GREW UP AMONG THEM. RABBAN SHIMON BEN GAMLIEL: NO COURT SITS WITHOUT THE PEOPLE MURMURING — WHY DOES THIS ONE SIT AND THAT ONE NOT? ({SP_(13, 4, "אבל", "אתם", "מכירים", "אותו", "שאתם", "גדלתם", "ביניהם")} "but you know him, for you grew up among them") — \'known\' read as the tribes\' own knowledge; the appointment by those who know.')
srow(13, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND I WILL SET THEM AS YOUR HEADS" — IF YOU APPOINTED THEM ARE THEY APPOINTED, AND IF NOT, NOT? "I WILL SET THEM": IF I APPOINTED THEM THEY ARE APPOINTED. IF YOU MADE THEM GREAT ARE THEY GREAT? "I WILL SET THEM": IF I MADE THEM GREAT. ({SP_(13, 5, "אם", "מניתים", "הרי", "הם", "ממונים")} "if I appointed them, they are appointed") — the appointment Moses\' alone; the English reads the alternatives as the Teaching\'s answers.')
srow(13, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: IF YOU GUARD YOUR WORDS, YOUR HEADS ARE GUARDED. ANOTHER WORD: READ NOT "I WILL SET THEM AS YOUR HEADS" BUT "THEIR GUILT ON YOUR HEADS" — ISRAEL\'S GUILT HANGS ON THE HEADS OF THEIR JUDGES; "SON OF MAN, I HAVE MADE YOU A WATCHMAN... IF YOU WARN THE WICKED" (Ezekiel 33:7-9). THE REVOCALIZATION ROW ({SP_(13, 6, "אל", "תהי", "קורא", "ואשימם", "בראשיכם", "אלא")} "read not \'I will set them as your heads\' but" — \'their guilt\' by the same consonants): the store\'s \'and-put/set-them\' read by another pointing; the middah: the AL TIKREI (read not thus but thus) — the aggadic move on the consonants, to check against MOVE_CATALOG; the watchman of Ezekiel 33 the judge\'s liability (9:2\'s kin).')
srow(14, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU ANSWERED ME: THE THING YOU SPOKE IS GOOD TO DO" — YOU SHOULD HAVE SAID: MOSES, FROM WHOM IS IT FIT TO LEARN TORAH — FROM YOU, WHO SUFFERED FOR IT FORTY DAYS AND NIGHTS, OR FROM YOUR DISCIPLE\'S DISCIPLE? BUT I KNOW WHAT IS UNDER YOUR HEELS: YOU SAID, NOW HE APPOINTS EIGHTY THOUSAND JUDGES LESS A FEW; IF NOT I, MY SON; WE BRING HIM A GIFT AND HE FAVORS US. WHEN I WAS SLOW YOU SAID: LET IT BE DONE QUICKLY! THE ROW WITHOUT A HEAD CITATION (it continues 1:14: {SP_(14, 1, "שמונים", "אלף", "חסר", "פרוטרוט")} "eighty thousand less a fraction" — the judges counted: 600 captains of thousands, 6,000 of hundreds, 12,000 of fifties, 60,000 of tens — 78,600, \'eighty thousand less a few\'): the people\'s eagerness read as the hope of bribable courts; THE COMPILE\'S ARITHMETIC — the officers\' count from the census (the parser\'s [100, 50, 10] with the thousands as a noun).')
srow(15, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND I TOOK THE HEADS OF YOUR TRIBES, WISE MEN... AND I CHARGED YOUR JUDGES" (1:15-16) — I DREW THEM WITH WORDS: HAPPY ARE YOU! OVER WHOM ARE YOU APPOINTED? OVER THE SONS OF ABRAHAM, ISAAC AND JACOB, CALLED BROTHERS AND FRIENDS, A DESIRABLE VINEYARD, AN INHERITANCE, THE FLOCK OF HIS PASTURE — EVERY TERM OF LOVE. ({SP_(15, 1, "משכתים", "בדברים", "אמרתי", "להם", "אשריכם")} "I drew them with words; I said to them: happy are you") — the head on two verses; the judges persuaded to serve.')
srow(15, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"WISE AND KNOWN MEN" — THIS IS ONE OF THE SEVEN QUALITIES JETHRO TOLD MOSES; HE WENT AND FOUND ONLY THREE: WISE AND KNOWN MEN. ({SP_(15, 2, "הלך", "ולא", "מצא", "אלא", "שלש")} "he went and found only three") — THE INK: Exodus 18:21\'s four (able, God-fearing, true, hating gain), 1:13\'s three (wise, understanding, known), 1:15\'s two — the Sifrei counts seven across both and finds three (men, wise, known); the compile\'s docket: the qualities as a checklist against the appointments.')
srow(15, 3, 'CONTEXT', '"AND I MADE THEM HEADS OVER YOU" — HONORED BY YOU: HEADS IN BUYING, IN SELLING, IN TRADE, IN ENTERING AND LEAVING — FIRST IN, LAST OUT. The heads\' honor.')
srow(15, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"CAPTAINS OF THOUSANDS" — IF THERE WERE 1,999 ONLY A CAPTAIN OF A THOUSAND IS TAKEN; "OF HUNDREDS" — 199, ONE OF A HUNDRED; "OF FIFTIES" — 99, ONE OF FIFTY; "OF TENS" — 19, ONE OF TEN. THE ROUNDING ROW ({SP_(15, 4, "שאם", "היו", "אלף", "תשע", "מאות", "ותשעים", "ותשעה")} "that if there were a thousand nine hundred and ninety-nine") — the captains counted by whole units, the remainder unled: THE COMPILE\'S RULE for the officers\' table (integer division at four grains).')
srow(15, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND OFFICERS" — THESE ARE THE LEVITES WHO STRIKE WITH THE STRAP ("THE OFFICERS, THE LEVITES, BEFORE YOU", 2 Chronicles 19:11; "THE LEVITES QUIETED THE PEOPLE", Nehemiah 8:11). ({SP_(15, 5, "אלו", "הלוים", "המכים", "ברצועה")} "these are the Levites who strike with the strap") — the officers-word (thirteen Torah seats: Exodus 5\'s foremen, 16:18\'s appointment) given a tribe and an instrument; the compile\'s officer.')
srow(16, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND I CHARGED YOUR JUDGES: HEAR BETWEEN YOUR BROTHERS AND JUDGE RIGHTEOUSLY" — I SAID: BE DELIBERATE IN JUDGMENT; IF A CASE COMES BEFORE YOU TWICE AND THRICE, SAY NOT "IT CAME ALREADY", BUT BE DELIBERATE. SO THE MEN OF THE GREAT ASSEMBLY (Avot 1:1): BE DELIBERATE IN JUDGMENT, RAISE MANY DISCIPLES, MAKE A FENCE FOR THE TORAH. ({SP_(16, 1, "היו", "מתונים", "בדין")} "be deliberate in judgment") — AVOT 1:1\'s first saying seated on 1:16: the testing shelf\'s own maxim read as this verse\'s charge (the Mishnah cited by the Sifrei — the bridge the compile keeps).')
srow(16, 2, 'CONTEXT', '"AT THAT TIME, SAYING" — BEFORE, YOU WERE YOUR OWN; NOW YOU ARE SERVANTS BOUND TO THE PUBLIC. The judge indentured.')
srow(16, 3, 'CONTEXT', 'THE STORY OF R. YOHANAN BEN NURI AND R. ELAZAR HISMA, SEATED BY RABBAN GAMLIEL AND UNNOTICED BY THE DISCIPLES; THEY SAT AMONG THE DISCIPLES; GAMLIEL: YOU HAVE HARMED THE PUBLIC, WHO DO NOT SEEK TO RULE OVER IT — BEFORE YOU WERE YOUR OWN, HENCEFORTH SERVANTS BOUND TO THE PUBLIC. The case of 16:2.')
srow(16, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"HEAR BETWEEN YOUR BROTHERS" — R. ISHMAEL\'S WAY: WHEN AN ISRAELITE AND A GENTILE CAME BEFORE HIM, IF BY ISRAEL\'S LAW HE ACQUITTED THE ISRAELITE, IF BY THE NATIONS\' LAW HE ACQUITTED THE ISRAELITE — "WHAT DO I CARE? THE TORAH SAID: HEAR BETWEEN YOUR BROTHERS". RABBAN SHIMON BEN GAMLIEL: NO NEED — IF THEY CAME BY ISRAEL\'S LAW HE JUDGED BY ISRAEL\'S, BY THE NATIONS\' BY THE NATIONS\'. THE DISPUTE ROW ({SP_(16, 4, "אם", "בא", "לדון", "בדיני", "ישראל")} "if he came to be judged by Israel\'s laws") — \'your brothers\' read for the gentile litigant two ways; the compile\'s docket flags the dispute (the two rulings as two verdict tables).')
srow(16, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"JUDGE RIGHTEOUSLY" — THE RIGHTEOUS CLAIMANT IN HIS RIGHT CLAIMS AND BRINGS PROOFS. A PARABLE: THIS ONE WRAPPED IN HIS CLOAK AND THAT ONE SAYS IT IS MINE; PLOWING WITH HIS COW; HOLDING HIS FIELD; SITTING IN HIS HOUSE — AND THAT ONE SAYS IT IS MINE. ({SP_(16, 5, "צדיק", "בצדקו", "תובע", "ומביא", "ראיות")} "the righteous in his right claims and brings proofs") — possession against the claim: the burden of proof on the claimant (the compile\'s rule: the holder holds).')
srow(16, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"BETWEEN A MAN" — TO EXCLUDE THE MINOR; HENCE: ORPHANS ARE NOT JUDGED. ({SP_(16, 6, "להוציא", "את", "הקטן")} "to exclude the minor") — the exclusion (I2) from \'a man\'.')
srow(16, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"BETWEEN A MAN AND HIS BROTHER" — ONLY BETWEEN MAN AND MAN? BETWEEN MAN AND WOMAN, WOMAN AND MAN, NATION AND FAMILY, FAMILY AND FAMILY? "BETWEEN A MAN AND HIS BROTHER" — IN EVERY CASE. ({SP_(16, 7, "בין", "איש", "ובין", "אחיו", "מכל", "מקום")} "between a man and his brother — in every case") — the inclusion (I2) from the second clause.')
srow(16, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HIS STRANGER" — HE WHO PILES UP WORDS AGAINST HIM: YOU PLOWED A FURROW IN MY FIELD — I DID NOT; YOUR OX KILLED MY OX — IT DID NOT; YOUR OX KILLED MY SLAVE — IT DID NOT. ({SP_(16, 8, "זה", "שאוגר", "עליו", "דברים")} "this is one who piles up words against him") — the stranger-word read by its sound (\'piles up\'): the denier of claims; the ink: \'his stranger\' two Bible seats.')
srow(16, 9, 'CONTEXT', 'ANOTHER WORD: "HIS STRANGER" — HIS NEIGHBOR; ANOTHER: HIS GROOMSMAN; ANOTHER: HIS LODGER. The four readings.')
srow(17, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT RECOGNIZE FACES IN JUDGMENT" — THIS IS THE ONE APPOINTED TO SEAT JUDGES: LEST YOU SAY, THIS MAN IS HANDSOME, STRONG, MY KINSMAN, HE LENT ME MONEY, HE KNOWS LANGUAGES — I WILL SEAT HIM; HE ACQUITS THE GUILTY AND CONVICTS THE INNOCENT, NOT FROM WICKEDNESS BUT IGNORANCE — IT IS COUNTED AS IF HE RECOGNIZED FACES. ({SP_(17, 1, "זה", "הממנה", "להושיב", "דינים")} "this is the one appointed to seat judges") — the prohibition moved from the judge to the appointer; the ink: the clause 1:17 and 16:19.')
srow(17, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"SMALL AND GREAT ALIKE YOU SHALL HEAR" — LEST YOU SAY: THIS ONE IS POOR AND THE RICH MAN IS BOUND TO SUPPORT HIM; I WILL ACQUIT HIM AND HE IS SUPPORTED HONORABLY. ({SP_(17, 2, "הואיל", "ועני", "זה", "עשיר", "זה", "מצוה", "לפרנסו")} "since this one is poor, this rich one is bound to support him") — the poor man\'s favor refused (Exodus 23:3\'s kin).')
srow(17, 3, 'CONTEXT', 'ANOTHER WORD: LEST YOU SAY: HOW CAN I SHAME THIS RICH MAN FOR A DINAR? I WILL ACQUIT HIM AND TELL HIM OUTSIDE TO PAY. THE RICH MAN\'S DIGNITY REFUSED. (The pair with 17:2.)')
srow(17, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT BE AFRAID OF A MAN" — WHEN TWO COME BEFORE YOU, BEFORE YOU HEAR THEM YOU MAY BE SILENT; ONCE YOU HAVE HEARD, YOU MAY NOT ("BEFORE THE QUARREL BREAKS OUT, LEAVE OFF", Proverbs 17:14). IF YOU HEARD AND DO NOT KNOW HOW TO ACQUIT OR CONVICT, YOU MAY BE SILENT — "TRUTH AND THE JUDGMENT OF PEACE" (Zechariah 8:16): WHICH PEACE HAS JUDGMENT? COMPROMISE. RABBAN SHIMON BEN GAMLIEL: RAISING THE SMALL AND LOWERING THE GREAT IS COMPROMISE; THE SAGES: WHOEVER COMPROMISES SINS — "HE WHO BLESSES A COMPROMISER SPURNS THE LORD" (Psalm 10:3). THE COMPROMISE DISPUTE ({SP_(17, 4, "עד", "שלא", "תשמע", "לדבריהם", "אתה", "רשי", "לשתוק")} "before you hear their words you may be silent"; {SP_(17, 4, "כל", "המבצע", "הרי", "זה", "חוטא")} "whoever compromises, he sins") — the timing of silence and the standing dispute on arbitration (Sanhedrin 6b\'s sugya the bridge); the compile\'s docket flags it.')
srow(17, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT BE AFRAID OF A MAN" — LEST YOU SAY: I FEAR THIS MAN, LEST HE KILL MY SON, BURN MY STACK, CUT MY PLANTS — "FOR THE JUDGMENT IS GOD\'S". ({SP_(17, 5, "שמא", "יהרג", "את", "בני")} "lest he kill my son") — the fear-verb read (the store\'s sojourn-gloss corrected by reference in the ink); \'the judgment is God\'s\' the ground.')
srow(17, 6, 'CONTEXT', 'SO JEHOSHAPHAT: "SEE WHAT YOU DO, FOR YOU JUDGE NOT FOR MAN BUT FOR THE LORD" (2 Chronicles 19:6). The proof.')
srow(17, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE MATTER TOO HARD FOR YOU" — THE HOLY ONE TO MOSES: YOU JUDGE A HARD CASE? BY YOUR LIFE, I WILL BRING A CASE YOUR DISCIPLE\'S DISCIPLE CAN HEAR AND YOU CANNOT — THE DAUGHTERS OF ZELOPHEHAD: "MOSES BROUGHT THEIR CASE BEFORE THE LORD" (Numbers 27:5). SO SAMUEL: "I AM THE SEER" (1 Samuel 9:19) — YOU SEE? "LOOK NOT ON HIS APPEARANCE" (16:7). THE HARD MATTER ROW ({SP_(17, 7, "זה", "דינן", "של", "בנות", "צלפחד")} "this is the case of the daughters of Zelophehad") — THE TENT\'S fourth sitting (Numbers 27, num_27_zelophehad_joshua, frozen and compiled) named as the case Moses could not hear: the link from 1:17 to the daughters\' case a REFERENCE the Sifrei itself teaches (LR1: a teacher taught it).')
assert sorted(S) == [(p, r) for p in range(9, 18) for r in range(1, SIF_ROWS[p] + 1)], sorted(S)
